/** @mainpage Qore protobuf Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section protobufintro protobuf Module Introduction

    The \c protobuf module provides dynamic Protocol Buffer schema loading, encoding,
    and decoding for Qore. It wraps Google's libprotobuf library to provide:

    - Loading schemas from <tt>.proto</tt> files, strings, serialized descriptors, or
      programmatic hash definitions
    - Encoding Qore hashes to protobuf binary format
    - Decoding protobuf binary data to Qore hashes
    - JSON conversion via protobuf's canonical JSON format
    - Schema introspection (message types, field metadata, enum values, services)
    - File descriptor serialization for schema transport and reconstruction

    @section protobufqlibmodules Qore User Modules

    - @ref connectintro "Connect" — streaming RPC over HTTP with YAML serialization and gRPC compatibility
    - @ref qoreonnxexportintro "QoreOnnxExport" — ONNX model export for trained ML models

    @section protobufdocumentation Documentation

    - @anchor protobuftype @subpage protobuftypeguide
    - @anchor protobuferrors @subpage protobuferrorsguide
    - @anchor protobufexamples @subpage protobufexamplesguide
    - @anchor protobufrelnotes @subpage protobufreleasehistory

    @section protobufnesting Nested Messages

    A message field that is not set has no value in a hash (@ref nothing), so a message type that contains a field of
    its own type, directly or through other message types, has a finite default message.  Messages are converted to
    and from hashes to 100 levels of messages below the top-level message (an entry of a map field is a level, as in
    protobuf), the default recursion limit of protobuf's binary and JSON parsers: deeper data raises
    \c PROTOBUF-DEPTH-ERROR (data from outside the program nested deeper than the parsers allow raises
    \c PROTOBUF-DECODE-ERROR or \c PROTOBUF-JSON-ERROR), and the conversion also stops with
    \c STACK-LIMIT-EXCEEDED if the thread's stack would be exhausted.

